{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GmRY5gig3pMYAghg9K3KFz","type":"tool_result","content":"    \"P3\": dict(world=\"real\", searcher=\"exhaustive\", K=24, N=200, R=30),\n    \"P4\": dict(world=\"real\", searcher=\"halving\", K=24, N=200, R=30),\n    \"P5\": dict(world=\"real\", searcher=\"exhaustive\", K=24, N=60, R=30),\n    \"P6\": dict(world=\"real\", searcher=\"exhaustive\", K=24, N=600, R=30),\n    \"N1\": dict(world=\"syn_null\", searcher=\"exhaustive\", K=32, N=150, R=30),\n    \"N2\": dict(world=\"real_null\", searcher=\"exhaustive\", K=24, N=200, R=30),\n    \"Z1\": dict(world=\"const\", searcher=\"exhaustive\", K=8, N=100, R=10),\n}\nSMOKE_N = {\"syn\": 40, \"syn_null\": 40, \"real\": 30, \"real_null\": 30, \"const\": 20}\nSMOKE_POOL = 150\nSMOKE_R = 2\n\n\ndef case_params(name, smoke):\n    p = dict(CASES[name])\n18,28c18,20\n< distribution).  Calibration: a parametric bootstrap on the fitted model.  Synthetic worlds\n< (a*, b*, subject means, s*) are drawn from the fitted posterior, outcomes are simulated on the\n< SAME (question, config) design as the log, the model is refit (few warm-started Newton sweeps at\n< fixed tau2/s2) and the pivot error theta*_k - theta_hat*_k of the selected config is recorded.\n< Its empirical 5%/95% quantiles give asymmetric offsets around the plug-in estimate and its\n< (clipped) median corrects residual bias.  Half-widths are floored at a fraction of the plain\n< posterior half-widths and mildly inflated on real (multi-subject) data, where a 1-D latent\n< difficulty model may be misspecified in ways the bootstrap cannot see.  If fewer than\n< _MIN_BOOT replicates finish (wall-clock guard) or anything fails, the earlier kappa-widened\n< posterior-quantile interval is used.  Degenerate worlds (all-zero outcomes, unobserved selected\n< config, tau2 at its lower clamp) are handled explicitly.\n---\n> distribution); the report is the 5% / 95% quantiles, widened around the estimate by a\n> calibration factor kappa.  Degenerate worlds (all-zero outcomes, unobserved selected config,\n> tau2 at its lower clamp) and a wall-clock guard are handled explicitly.\n52,61d43\n< _BOOT_B = 40              # maximum parametric-bootstrap replicates\n< _MIN_BOOT = 8             # fewer finished replicates -> kappa fallback\n< _BOOT_BUDGET_S = 3.0      # wall-clock guard for the bootstrap loop\n< _TOTAL_BUDGET_S = 5.5     # wall-clock guard for the whole report call\n< _REFIT_SWEEPS = 4         # warm-started Newton sweeps per bootstrap refit\n< _BIAS_CLIP = 0.02         # max |bias shift| applied to the estimate\n< _WIDTH_FLOOR = 0.85       # half-width >= floor * plain posterior half-width\n< _REAL_INFLATION = 1.05    # mild misspecification inflation on multi-subject (real) data\n< _EMP_WEIGHT = 0.7         # weight of empirical quantiles vs normal-score smoothing\n< \n131,198c113\n<     return {\"a\": a, \"b\": b, \"m\": m, \"tau2\": tau2, \"s2\": s2, \"S0\": S0, \"Hb\": Hb}\n< \n< \n< def _theta_of(a, m, shift, s, pi, x, wq):\n<     \"\"\"Fresh-question accuracy E_b[sigmoid(a - b)] for draws (a, shift, s) of shape (D,).\"\"\"\n<     z = (a[:, None, None] - m[None, :, None] - shift[:, None, None]\n<          - s[:, None, None] * x[None, None, :])\n<     return np.einsum(\"dsj,j,s->d\", _expit(z), wq, pi)\n< \n< \n< def _refit_fixed_var(q, c, y, sj, N, K, a0, b0, m0, tau2, s2, nsub, nsq):\n<     \"\"\"Warm-started damped Newton sweeps on (a, b) with fixed tau2/s2; returns a, b, m.\"\"\"\n<     yf = y.astype(np.float64)\n<     a = a0.copy()\n<     b = b0.copy()\n<     m = m0.copy()\n<     for _ in range(_REFIT_SWEEPS):\n<         p = _expit(a[c] - b[q])\n<         r = yf - p\n<         w = p * (1.0 - p)\n<         ga = np.bincount(c, r, K) - a / tau2\n<         Ha = np.bincount(c, w, K) + 1.0 / tau2\n<         a = a + np.clip(ga / Ha, -1.0, 1.0)\n<         p = _expit(a[c] - b[q])\n<         r = yf - p\n<         w = p * (1.0 - p)\n<         gb = -np.bincount(q, r, N) - (b - m[sj]) / s2\n<         Hb = np.bincount(q, w, N) + 1.0 / s2\n<         b = b + np.clip(gb / Hb, -1.0, 1.0)\n<         m = (np.bincount(sj, b, nsub) + _SUBJ_SHRINK * b.mean()) / (nsq + _SUBJ_SHRINK)\n<     return a, b, m\n< \n< \n< def _param_bootstrap(q, c, y, sj, N, K, k, fit, tau2_eff, pi, x, wq, nsub, rng, deadline):\n<     \"\"\"Pivot errors theta*_k - theta_hat*_k from synthetic worlds on the observed design.\"\"\"\n<     M = y.shape[0]\n<     s2 = fit[\"s2\"]\n<     s_hat = math.sqrt(s2)\n<     S_all = fit[\"S0\"] + 1.0 / tau2_eff\n<     a_mean_all = fit[\"a\"] * (fit[\"S0\"] + 1.0 / fit[\"tau2\"]) / S_all\n<     a_sd_all = 1.0 / np.sqrt(S_all)\n<     b_sd = 1.0 / np.sqrt(fit[\"Hb\"])\n<     m_hat = fit[\"m\"]\n<     nsq = np.maximum(np.bincount(sj, minlength=nsub).astype(np.float64), 1e-9)\n<     m_sd = s_hat / np.sqrt(nsq + _SUBJ_SHRINK)\n<     zero1 = np.zeros(1)\n<     errs = []\n<     for r in range(_BOOT_B):\n<         if r >= _MIN_BOOT and time.perf_counter() > deadline:\n<             break\n<         a_star = a_mean_all + a_sd_all * rng.standard_normal(K)\n<         b_star = fit[\"b\"] + b_sd * rng.standard_normal(N)\n<         s_star = s_hat * math.exp(rng.standard_normal() / math.sqrt(2.0 * max(N, 2)))\n<         if nsub > 1:\n<             m_star = m_hat + m_sd * rng.standard_normal(nsub)\n<         else:\n<             m_star = m_hat + s_hat * rng.standard_normal() / math.sqrt(max(N, 1))\n<         theta_true = float(_theta_of(a_star[k:k + 1], m_star, zero1, np.array([s_star]),\n<                                      pi, x, wq)[0])\n<         y_star = (rng.random(M) < _expit(a_star[c] - b_star[q])).astype(np.int64)\n<         a_r, b_r, m_r = _refit_fixed_var(q, c, y_star, sj, N, K, fit[\"a\"], fit[\"b\"], m_hat,\n<                                          tau2_eff, s2, nsub, nsq)\n<         theta_hat = float(_theta_of(a_r[k:k + 1], m_r, zero1, np.array([s_hat]),\n<                                     pi, x, wq)[0])\n<         errs.appen