ne in all eight seeds with paired differences 0.075, 0.053, 0.101.\",[ep]),\n E(\"Replayed naive Wilson coverage is 0.713 (sd 0.048) and width 0.109; Bonferroni-Wilson coverage 0.962, width 0.190; resampling coverage 0.748, width 0.104 (aggregate over P1-P6). The replay reproduces all recorded baseline interval scores and biases exactly.\",[ep,\"final.metric.naive_baseline_score\"]),\n E(\"Naive bias on real exhaustive cases falls with N: 0.051 (N=60), 0.022 (N=200), 0.009 (N=600).\",[ep]),\n E(\"Final-pool configuration accuracies range from 0.107 to 0.166 (task manifest); naive optimism at N=60 (0.051) is comparable to that spread.\",[ep]),\n E(\"Naive bias in null worlds: 0.067 in N1 vs 0.049 in P1; 0.034 in N2 vs 0.022 in P3.\",[ep]),\n E(\"Searcher effect on naive bias: P2 0.054, P4 0.025 vs P1 0.049, P3 0.022; matched paired differences +0.004 (sd 0.012) and +0.003 (sd 0.008); aggregated naive bias 0.036 for both searchers.\",[ep]),\n E(\"Per-case EB-IRT vs naive interval scores: P1 0.150 vs 0.264, P2 0.155 vs 0.300, P5 0.192 vs 0.303; reductions of 37-48%; coverage 0.96, 0.96, 0.98.\",[ep]),\n E(\"P4: EB-IRT 0.156 vs naive 0.161 and Bonferroni 0.165; wins in six of eight seeds; bias 0.031 vs 0.025; coverage 0.89. P6: all Wilson-style reporters 0.096; coverage 0.83.\",[ep]),\n E(\"Exhaustive-search restricted aggregate: EB-IRT 0.1406, resampling 0.1405, naive 0.2166; halving cases: resampling 0.3916 vs EB-IRT 0.1556.\",[ep]),\n E(\"Resampling is slightly better than EB-IRT in P3 (0.109 vs 0.116), P5 (0.174 vs 0.192) and N2 (0.102 vs 0.111); EB-IRT better in 2, 1 and 1 of 8 seeds.\",[ep]),\n E(\"Resampling over-corrects under halving: bias -0.067 (P2) and -0.031 (P4); coverage 0.44 and 0.61.\",[ep]),\n E(\"EB-IRT signed bias positive in five of six primary cases (0.009-0.031) and -0.002 (sd 0.010) in P1.\",[ep]),\n E(\"Interval widths at N=60/200/600: EB-IRT 0.187/0.101/0.065, naive 0.167/0.088/0.050, Bonferroni-Wilson 0.284/0.153/0.088.\",[ep]),\n E(\"Controls